nsferred.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 1","sha256":"bce112c1f2bf40fc0f5c46d5570e27ca01f4d362c30d9b2024e1468e4c280a52","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-12570-delegating-authority-implement-assistance-for-central-american"},"scope_id":"EO:12570#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. The Secretary of State is authorized to perform the following functions vested in the President by sections 205 and 206 of title II of the Military Construction Appropriations Act, 1987:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"bce112c1f2bf40fc0f5c46d5570e27ca01f4d362c30d9b2024e1468e4c280a52","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-12570-delegating-authority-implement-assistance-for-central-american"},"scope_id":"EO:12570#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 205, the authority to designate the account to which funds transferred from the funds appropriated by the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 1985 (Public Law 99-88), under the heading \"Assistance for Implementation of a Contadora Agreement,\" are deposited, and the amount transferred; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"bce112c1f2bf40fc0f5c46d5570e27ca01f4d362c30d9b2024e1468e4c280a52","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-12570-delegating-authority-implement-assistance-for-central-american"},"scope_id":"EO:12570#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The authority to implement section 206 utilizing the funds described in section 3 of this Order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"bce112c1f2bf40fc0f5c46d5570e27ca01f4d362c30d9b2024e1468e4c280a52","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-12570-delegating-authority-implement-assistance-for-central-american"},"scope_id":"EO:12570#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. The Secretary of Defense is authorized to perform the function, vested in the President by section 206 of title II of the Military Construction Appropriations Act, 1987, of designating the accounts from which unobligated funds, made available by the Department of Defense Appropriations Act, 1986 (as contained in Public Law 99190), are transferred.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 3","sha256":"bce112c1f2bf40fc0f5c46d5570e27ca01f4d362c30d9b2024e1468e4c280a52","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-12570-delegating-authority-implement-assistance-for-central-american"},"scope_id":"EO:12570#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"51 FR 39355, PDF pages 7-7","sha256":"905f08bc77f13d2ebaec70aea3b75b600078e75129a84921fb3ac73826ceccd3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1986-10-28/pdf/FR-1986-10-28.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 5 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_orde